settings.description:
Per-device overrides, keyed by numeric device id. Free-form, because the options a device accepts depend on what it is — edit this in the JSON config rather than here.

```json
"settings": {
  "1234567": { "name": "Kitchen blind" },
  "1234568": { "trigger": true },
  "1234569": { "delay": 10000, "autoCloseDelay": 300000 },
  "1657464": {
    "pin": "1234",
    "sensors": true,
    "aliases": { "stay": [1], "night": [1, 2] }
  }
}
```

`name` renames the accessory and `category` pins it to a HAP category, bypassing hardware detection. `trigger` turns a switch into a stateless one that returns to off. On a garage door, `delay` is the travel time in **milliseconds** (default 20000) and `autoCloseDelay` closes it again after that many milliseconds. `smokeDetector` publishes a temperature sensor as a smoke detector. `lightSensor` publishes a temperature sensor as an ambient light sensor, reading `lightPower`. On an alarm: `pin` overrides the platform PIN, `sensors: false` drops the companion accessory that holds one contact sensor per opening detector (it is published by default), `aliases` says which armed-zone combinations HomeKit should show as Home and Night, and `legacy` selects the CTX60 protocol (detected automatically; only set it if detection is wrong).
